  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 944 PM CST Wed Nov 18 2026\n\nWe'll undergo a pattern change this weekend that will bring rain \nchances back into the forecast. A trough will push a cold front \nthrough the area Sunday with widespread medium (40-60%) rain \nchances. A narrow band of better moisture will develop just ahead \nof the front, but instability looks very limited which will \ninhibit efficient rainfall and thunderstorm activity. As such, QPF\nvalues are very low, generally a tenth of an inch or less. The\nfront will clear the area Monday, bringing cool and dry conditions\nin through Tuesday. Highs will be in the 50s and overnight lows\nwill be in the 30s. We'll have another low chance for rain on \nWednesday, but ensembles show a larger spread of potential \noutcomes since models differ on where the upper low will track. \nGiven the uncertainty, low 15-25% rain chances remain in the \nforecast for next Wednesday. As for Thanksgiving, things are \ntrending dry right now for us, but it will be chilly. Highs will\nmaybe reach around 50 degrees, and overnight lows will fall into \nthe 20s, so be sure to dress warm!",
